# SoMe App — source of truth

Wire-like chat + community-scoped profiles. Not Pintap. Not a payments or dating marketplace.

Read when the task needs it: `docs/backend-design.md` (decisions D1–D25 + schema), spec v0.33, meeting transcript, mockup `SoMe App 260922`, Peter's drafts A19–A33, `docs/User-Stories-and-Requirements.tex`.

## Invariants (never violate)

- Scope every member/chat/search/schema query by **current `community_id`**.
- Group ≠ community. Group = chat room inside one community.
- Profile fields are **defs + values**, not hardcoded columns.
- "Real" image (formerly "verified") = in-app camera + date. Gallery photos allowed everywhere, never Real. Do not claim it cannot be faked.
- Private notes/ratings: author-only in UI **and** API.
- Group create = community admin, or members with group-create rights. One admin per group for now.
- Status (per-community list) decides which profile fields a member sees.

## Stop — do not implement

**Later:** payments, Swish, reputation, push, video/audio, co-admins, Google login, cross-community search, km distance. (Profile score is V1; rule = open question Q2.)

**Decided (Oct 2026):** 3 tabs Chats/Profiles/Ads; path `/{community}`; separate account per community (one login per email); Ads tab kept (A6–D3); fields built by the admin.

**TBD, ask:** user levels 1–3. Q1–Q8 in `docs/backend-design.md` §13 use their listed defaults.

If sources conflict, name the conflict. Do not pick a winner.
